#: bal/core/explainer.py:33
msgid "Write your will: choose the heirs and the date"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:34
msgid "In the software you write who inherits your bitcoin and from which date. Your bitcoin are recorded on the blockchain, at your address, and they stay yours."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:37
msgid "One copy for each will-executor, valid from the date you chose"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:38
msgid "Today the software signs one copy for each will-executor. It is like a post-dated cheque: it takes the bitcoin to your heirs, but the network accepts it only from the date you chose."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:41
msgid "Each will-executor keeps a copy, with its own fee"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:42
msgid "Each will-executor receives and keeps its copy. It does not have your keys: it can neither change the copy nor spend your bitcoin. Each copy contains a small fee, its pay, paid only on the delivery day."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:46
msgid "While you are here, nothing is sent: the bitcoin stay yours"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:47
msgid "Your bitcoin stay at your address and you use them as always. Until the delivery date, the will-executors send nothing and no bitcoin leaves your address."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:50
msgid "The delivery date arrives"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:51
msgid "The calendar reaches the date you chose. From that day the copy can be spent."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:53
msgid "On the chosen date, the copies are sent"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:54
msgid "Each will-executor takes its signed copy and sends it to the Bitcoin network, without needing you."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:56
msgid "The block accepts one copy only: the one sent first"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:57
msgid "The copies spend the same bitcoin, so the new block accepts only one of them, usually the one sent first. The other two wait in a row below the block."
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:60
msgid "Bitcoin to the heirs, fee to the will-executor; then the others lapse"
msgstr ""

#: bal/core/explainer.py:61
msgid "As soon as the copy is accepted, the bitcoin move from your address to your heirs' addresses, as set in the will, and a small fee goes to the will-executor whose copy was accepted. Only afterwards are the other two copies invalidated, because those bitcoin have already been spent."
msgstr ""

