#: bal/gui/qt/basic_wizard.py:158
msgid "Bitcoin counts time in <b>UTC</b>, Greenwich time, the same all over the world. Your computer's time zone can be ahead of it or behind it (Italy is 1 hour ahead in winter and 2 in summer). The will is saved in UTC: that is why the summary and the report show the UTC time.<br><b>If you are testing:</b> the Bitcoin network accepts the transaction only when the block clock has passed that time, usually about an hour later, sometimes more. Wait a few hours before thinking it did not work."
